WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.600
Welcome to Decision Analysis and Resolution. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Use explicit criteria to compare options and document important decisions.

2
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:21.770
Consider this scenario. A manager selects a supplier without an alternatives review. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:32.890
Start with two steps: Frame the decision and constraints. Then Set criteria before evaluating options. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:42.230
Continue with Compare credible alternatives. Then Record rationale and results. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:42.230 --> 00:01:02.820
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous decision record, criteria and scores, trade-off analysis tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: selecting the preferred option before establishing criteria; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:17.070
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
